\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Daily water-column conditions from January 2014 to December 2016 in the upper 1000\,m. The record is assembled from the ±20\,km box around EI (2014), KGI (January 2015 -- January 2016), and CI (February -- December 2016). Thin vertical black lines mark where the source site changes, and colored outlines mark each site's recording period. Top: sea-ice concentration (\%). Lower panels: potential temperature (°C), salinity, and dissolved oxygen (mmol\,m$^{-3}$) from the Copernicus Marine Service global physics reanalysis (temperature, salinity; 1/12°) and biogeochemistry hindcast (oxygen; 1/4°), plotted on a square-root depth axis with white contours (0.5\,°C, 0.1, and 20\,mmol m$^{-3}$, respectively). Dashed lines mark the boundaries of the surface (0--100\,m), mid-water (100--500\,m) and deep (500--1000\,m) layers; right-hand labels give the species whose foraging depths fall in each layer (Pm, sperm whale; Gm, long-finned pilot whale; Oo, killer whale; BW29, southern bottlenose whale; BW37, BW37 beaked whale). Grey areas mark depths with no model water in the box; at KGI, oxygen is unavailable below 773\,m, so the deep-layer oxygen mean there covers 500--773\,m.}}{5}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sections}{{2}{5}{Daily water-column conditions from January 2014 to December 2016 in the upper 1000\unit {m}. The record is assembled from the ±20\unit {km} box around EI (2014), KGI (January 2015 -- January 2016), and CI (February -- December 2016). Thin vertical black lines mark where the source site changes, and colored outlines mark each site's recording period. Top: sea-ice concentration (\%). Lower panels: potential temperature (°C), salinity, and dissolved oxygen (mmol\unit {m$^{-3}$}) from the Copernicus Marine Service global physics reanalysis (temperature, salinity; 1/12°) and biogeochemistry hindcast (oxygen; 1/4°), plotted on a square-root depth axis with white contours (0.5\unit {°C}, 0.1, and 20\unit {mmol m$^{-3}$}, respectively). Dashed lines mark the boundaries of the surface (0--100\unit {m}), mid-water (100--500\unit {m}) and deep (500--1000\unit {m}) layers; right-hand labels give the species whose foraging depths fall in each layer (Pm, sperm whale; Gm, long-finned pilot whale; Oo, killer whale; BW29, southern bottlenose whale; BW37, BW37 beaked whale). Grey areas mark depths with no model water in the box; at KGI, oxygen is unavailable below 773\unit {m}, so the deep-layer oxygen mean there covers 500--773\unit {m}}{figure.caption.3}{}}
